  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target audience consists of internet users familiar with racial stereotypes and cyberbullying tropes, particularly those who understand and find humor in degrading Black individuals through absurd accusations. The meme relies on the audience’s implicit knowledge of anti-Black stereotypes (e.g., comparing Black people to primates, hypersexualization, criminal behavior associations) to generate its humor, making it primarily effective for viewers who accept or are aware of these prejudiced frameworks. The audience is likely to be online communities that engage in mocking or ridiculing public figures, especially Black men, using visual and textual memes that rely on racialized humor and humiliation.",
